# The one-instruction UCRT floor import thunk has 438 direct callers in the
# frozen PE.  The pixel-snap quad emitter (sub_0055f990) reaches it four times
# per snapped quad and sub_002daef0 twice; the sampler attributes 0.30 ms per
# room frame to the thunk, roughly half of it dispatch overhead
# (GUEST_IMPORT_JMP -> guest_import_call -> indexed family dispatch -> noinline
# stack helpers -> vita_math_floor).  The Vita math family already owns the
# exact cdecl/x87 semantics; the seam executes the same floor inline at the
# root when the slot token is still the authenticated floor import and the
# frame is inside the bound guest stack, and otherwise falls closed into the
# unchanged GUEST_IMPORT_JMP spelling.  Unlike the memset seam the text is a
# generation-time switch (GUEST_FLOOR_THUNK_FASTPATH=1) so a corpus generated
# without it stays byte-identical; the CMake option then activates the fenced
# seam, and an option-OFF object of a switched-on corpus is byte-identical
