# The shipping PCSB00676 app and its 1.05 patch both disable caustics,
# shockwave and the texture filter in resources/config_vita.ini while keeping
# lighting enabled.  Rebirth also predates Repentance's separate water-surface
# renderer entirely.  Repentance's PC OptionsConfig loader defaults every one
# of these fields to one when its desktop config omits the key, so our port was
# doing materially more effect work than the original Vita target.
#
# Apply the three common-to-both-Vita-revisions values and disable both the
# Repentance water-surface value and its copied latch immediately after the
# exact loader has parsed/stored them.  Also disable Repentance's separate
# whole-room ColorModifier capture/composite: unlike the already bypassed
# outer post-process surfaces, it still wraps Room::Render before HUD::Render
# and can replace the world with a black sampled surface on Vita.  Leave color
# correction and pixelation alone: those differ between the base app and
# patch.  The injection mutates no guest register and calls no helper; it is a
