# Entity_Laser::Render and Entity_Laser::RenderShadowLayer are the exact two
# generated owners needed to attribute the physical three-beam cliff.  This
# diagnostic deliberately does not change laser sampling, geometry, collision,
# or shadows.  The active-path seams run after each owner's visibility/sample
# guards; the paired end seams are the owners' common epilogues.  The guest EBP
# is a stable, recursion-safe invocation token until those epilogues restore it.
# In this frozen PE,
# sample byte +0x3ad selects the curved-capable path: Render accepts zero or
# positive values, while RenderShadowLayer accepts only positive values.  Thus
# a global "skip straight-laser shadows" policy cannot explain or fix the
# expensive non-sample path; physical counts must precede any visual policy.
