# ANM2::RenderLayer asks AnimationData::_layerMap for the storage order of a
# logical layer, then immediately indexes both AnimationState::_layerFrames and
# AnimationData::_animLayers with that signed value.  A missing layer is -1.
# Windows' LFH happens to put a negative metadata dword immediately before the
# one-element `_layerFrames` allocation, masking the bug; a normal Vita/newlib
# allocation does not.  Reject the sentinel at the semantic boundary instead
# of emulating an undocumented Windows heap layout.
#
# All three physical paths in the frozen owner are pinned.  The shared third
# path has already pushed EAX before loading the map value, so its skip edge
# must unwind exactly that one guest word.  The first two paths have pushed
# nothing yet.
