# FileManager::LoadArchiveFile registers each packed-archive index entry, then
# constructs a temporary ArchivedFile and decodes the complete entry solely to
# recompute its checksum.  The frozen executable carries an independent table
# of expected index checksums.  Immediately before the temporary constructor it
# records whether the entry's index checksum matches that baked table in byte
# +0x18.  Vita may skip only those independently matched entries; a zero byte
# retains the complete original constructor/read/checksum/destructor path.
#
# The synthetic x86 stack already contains the constructor's one 4-byte
# argument at the seam.  The opt-in edge must discard exactly that argument
# before joining the original hash-table insertion at 0x00563c8c.  It neither
# constructs nor destroys the temporary object, and it does not modify CPU
# registers, flags, the entry, or the archive index/hash tables.
