# Frozen whole-program result after generic strict-AND, bounded memory-reload
# guards, exact remaps, exact spill/reload packages and exact-site noreturn
# termination.  The generic reload proof remains capped at 64 slots; the one
# 201-slot Entity_Effect::Update dispatcher and all eight tables exposed by its
# fixed point are a separately pinned owner package.  Entity_Player::Update's
# split helper is another exact owner package: five remaps complete its eight
# reachable tables without broadening byte-map recognition globally.  The
# room-entry normaliser adds three exact remaps shared by its physical fragment
# and the logical Room::FixSpawnEntry entry body.  GridEntity_Rock::InitSubclass
# likewise contributes one exact ten-way remap to both of its generated roots.
# Entity_NPC::update_ai contributes its complete three-remap, 262-label owner.
# Room::render_entity_light contributes three newly recovered tables to its
# already-proved Type dispatcher, completing one 39-label logical body.
# Entity_Tear::reset_sprite_scale contributes the first split-register remap
# copied into its physical root and the preceding recursive-descent body.  The
# strict generic split-register proof initially accepts 35 further physical
# sites.  Entity_Tear::Update completes the live five-table owner, and the
# exact second Entity_Player helper makes both of its split sites canonical.
# The generic same-register proof now closes its exact 186-site final corpus.
# One tightly bounded frame-spill remap proof and the exact active-item owner
# close the Teleport 2.0 path; six unusual selector packages remain site-pinned.
# Twenty-five closed-set false metadata starts are removed only after their
# containing instructions/CFGs are re-proved.  One is additionally frozen as
# the exact ASCII `DAT\0` value seen at eleven aligned libpng `IDAT\0` tails;
# three more have one exact unrelocated data-word coincidence each, frozen with
# their surrounding string/packed-table bytes.  Those narrow exceptions do
# not weaken real pointer evidence.  Exact terminal call pins close every
# recovered case body without treating a common CRT helper as globally fatal.
