# Lua C functions are registered as pointers passed to lua_pushcclosure.  The
# frozen function metadata collapses some of those real entry points into
# larger owners, so a dispatch table built only from metadata roots cannot
# call every registered function back.  This census follows both direct IAT
# calls and register-loaded IAT calls, proves the cdecl callback argument, and
# emits only the callback entries missing from the canonical root set.
#
# Rows hashed below are little-endian uint32 tuples:
#   call:  owner, call, callback-push, callback-target, provenance, kind
#          (kind 0 = direct IAT, 1 = register loaded at provenance)
#   load:  owner, IAT-load
#   owner: callback-target, metadata-owner-begin, metadata-owner-end
