# The ordinary PC discovery path does not need the guest Lua VM yet.  Its
# first reserve is one GiB (with a 512 MiB fallback), and entering that path
# also reaches Windows allocator atomics which the translator cannot emit.
# Keep the already constructed manager object registered so the surrounding
# startup object's ownership remains coherent.  The default/no-Lua build skips
# both reservations and sub_003fcb00 (the Lua initializer).  ISAAC_VITA_LUA
# still skips the impossible 1 GiB/512 MiB reservations, publishes a null
# custom allocator, and rejoins at the original LuaEngine::Init call instead.
# That initializer then selects the bridge's bounded guest-heap luaL_newstate
# path and reaches the frozen RegisterClasses body.  This gate deliberately
# tests the selected backend mode, not backend readiness: the renderer cannot
# become ready until later startup code has run.
