# Application::Run contains three compiler-inlined copies of glfwGetTime.  A
# live Vita run proved that they are not dead copies: after entering a room the
# third one is the limiter's spin sample.  With GLFW deliberately absent it
# returns 0.0, the `ja 00476c10` backedge can never expire, and every spin logs
# GLFW_NOT_INITIALIZED.  Use the same checked backend clock as the public root
# at only these three exact sites.  The injected edge writes XMM0 and no other
# guest state; disabled execution falls through to all 96 original bytes.
